<!--
  SYNTHETIC — AND THE PROVENANCE GAP IS DELIBERATE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT.

  The r5 plan asks Task 2.4 for AUTHENTIC Djinni / WeWorkRemotely / EU-board feeds.
  Obtaining those means outbound GETs to live job boards, which this project requires
  the owner's explicit go for. So the one authentic-grammar feed in this corpus is the
  committed DOU sample (`../../__fixtures__/dou-feed.golden.xml`), and this file carries
  the SHAPES those three boards are documented to use, with field values invented.

  What it therefore proves: the port handles these structures. What it does NOT prove:
  that any of these boards actually emits them. Phase 3 re-acquires each feed under the
  plan's fixture protocol (provenance, date, hash) and this file is superseded then.

  STATUS, as of the 2026-10-21 review round (finding SPEC-M-1, left OPEN on purpose):
  **authentic feeds pending owner authorisation.** The review was explicit that this one
  must not be reported as done, and it is not: an outbound GET to a job board is an
  external send, which `.claude/rules/common/autonomy-levels.md` classes A3 —
  irreversible, requiring the owner's explicit authorisation, which has not been given.

  The failure mode to guard against is not the gap, it is the gap going quiet. Do NOT
  close SPEC-M-1 by adding more synthetic fixtures: that grows the corpus without
  growing the evidence, and leaves a larger file making the same weaker claim. The only
  thing that closes it is an authentic capture, and the only thing that unblocks that is
  the owner saying so.

  Shapes represented, each the thing the board is known for:
    - a `<group>` of items where one member is well-formed and another lacks a link
      (the plan's "partial group": one bad member must not void the rest);
    - the same item twice with a CHANGED description (the "updated descriptions" case);
    - a non-conventional namespace prefix for a standard vocabulary.
-->
